---
import Scenario from "../../components/Scenario.astro";
import Playground from "../../layouts/Playground.astro";
---

<Playground title="Scopes & nesting">
	<Fragment slot="intro">
		<p>
			A reference without a scope uses the nearest <code>data-store</code>
			ancestor. Prefix it with a scope to cross a store boundary:
			<code>profile:$name</code>, <code>profile:@rename</code> or
			<code>profile:#badge</code>. Every scope name must be unique on the page.
		</p>
	</Fragment>

	<Scenario
		id="nested"
		title="Nested stores use the nearest scope"
		description="Three nested stores each have `name` state and a `rename` action. Inner levels also read the outer store with `outer:$name` and call it with `outer:@rename`."
		expect={[
			"Each level's `$name` shows its own store's name.",
			"Each `Rename` button renames only its own level, even though every store has a `rename` action.",
			"`Rename outer` inside the innermost level renames the outer store, and every `outer:$name` follows.",
			"The outer store element's `data-name` attribute, bound with `data-bind--data-name`, follows its name.",
		]}
	>
		<div data-store="outer" data-bind--data-name="$name" class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-line p-4">
			<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold" data-dom--text="$name"></p>
				<button class="btn btn-sm ml-auto" data-events--click="@rename">Rename</button>
			</div>
			<div data-store="inner" class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-raised/40 p-4">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
					<p class="text-sm font-semibold" data-dom--text="$name"></p>
					<p class="text-xs text-subtle">inside <span data-dom--text="outer:$name"></span></p>
					<button class="btn btn-sm ml-auto" data-events--click="@rename">Rename</button>
				</div>
				<div data-store="innermost" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-raised p-4">
					<p class="text-sm font-semibold" data-dom--text="$name"></p>
					<p class="text-xs text-subtle">
						inside <span data-dom--text="inner:$name"></span>, inside
						<span data-dom--text="outer:$name"></span>
					</p>
					<div class="ml-auto flex gap-2">
						<button class="btn btn-sm" data-events--click="@rename">Rename</button>
						<button class="btn btn-sm" data-events--click="outer:@rename">Rename outer</button>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Scenario>

	<Scenario
		id="outside"
		title="References from outside a store"
		description="The `profile` store's element only holds its name. The line below sits outside every store, and the toolbar is another store; both read, call and register refs on `profile` with explicit scopes."
		expect={[
			"The outside line and the toolbar show the profile's greeting and visits.",
			"`Rename` and `Visit` outside the profile element change the profile's state.",
			"`Flash badge` runs a profile action that reaches the `#badge` ref registered from outside with `profile:#badge`, and toggles its highlight.",
			"The toolbar still reads its own `$title` while reading `profile:$name`.",
		]}
	>
		<div class="space-y-3">
			<div data-store="profile" class="rounded-md bg-raised px-3 py-2 text-sm">
				Profile store: <span class="font-medium" data-dom--text="$name"></span>
			</div>
			<p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted">
				<span data-dom--text="profile:$greeting"></span>
				<span class="font-mono text-xs">visits <span data-dom--text="profile:$visits"></span></span>
				<span class="badge data-highlighted:border-accent/50 data-highlighted:text-accent" data-ref="profile:#badge">badge</span>
				<button class="btn btn-sm ml-auto" data-events--click="profile:@rename">Rename</button>
				<button class="btn btn-sm" data-events--click="profile:@visit">Visit</button>
				<button class="btn btn-sm" data-events--click="profile:@flashBadge">Flash badge</button>
			</p>
			<div data-store="toolbar" class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-line px-3 py-2 text-sm">
				<span class="font-medium" data-dom--text="$title"></span>
				<span class="text-muted">signed in as <span data-dom--text="profile:$name"></span></span>
				<button class="btn btn-sm ml-auto" data-events--click="profile:@rename">Rename from the toolbar</button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Scenario>

	<Scenario
		id="unresolved"
		title="References that can't be resolved"
		description="Four references that point at nothing: an unscoped one outside any store, an unknown scope, unknown state on a real store, and an unknown action. A scope with no store isn't an error: the directive waits for that store, as in the next scenarios."
		expect={[
			"On load the log warns that Catalyst can't infer a store for `$name`.",
			"The log warns that there is no state `nickname` on the `profile` store.",
			"`profiel:$name` logs no warning. With Debug ticked, the log shows it waiting for a store with the scope `profiel`.",
			"All three lines stay empty and the rest of the page keeps working.",
			"Clicking `Call a missing action` warns that `missing` can't be found on `profile`.",
		]}
	>
		<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
			<li class="flex gap-3"><code>$name</code> <span class="text-muted" data-dom--text="$name"></span></li>
			<li class="flex gap-3"><code>profiel:$name</code> <span class="text-muted" data-dom--text="profiel:$name"></span></li>
			<li class="flex gap-3"><code>profile:$nickname</code> <span class="text-muted" data-dom--text="profile:$nickname"></span></li>
			<li><button class="btn btn-sm" data-events--click="profile:@missing">Call a missing action</button></li>
		</ul>
	</Scenario>

	<Scenario
		id="duplicates"
		title="Duplicate scopes"
		description={'Two elements use `data-store="duplicate"`. The second is skipped, and the directives inside it are left unbound, so its markup stays as it was rendered.'}
		expect={[
			"The first element shows `first element`, and its `Report` logs that label.",
			"The second element keeps its server text `not bound`, and its `Report` does nothing.",
			"The log shows one warning: the `duplicate` scope is already used by another element, so that element and its directives are skipped.",
		]}
	>
		<div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
			<div data-store="duplicate" data-state--label="first element" class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md bg-raised px-3 py-2">
				<span class="text-sm" data-dom--text="$label">not bound</span>
				<button class="btn btn-sm ml-auto" data-events--click="@report">Report</button>
			</div>
			<div data-store="duplicate" data-state--label="second element" class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md bg-raised px-3 py-2">
				<span class="text-sm" data-dom--text="$label">not bound</span>
				<button class="btn btn-sm ml-auto" data-events--click="@report">Report</button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Scenario>

	<Scenario
		id="late-store"
		title="A store that appears later"
		description="The line and button below reference `late:` before any `late` element exists. Directives for a missing store are left as they are until a sync creates it. The plain JavaScript buttons insert the store's markup and call `Catalyst.sync`, or remove it."
		expect={[
			"On load the line keeps its server text, `Waiting for the late store…`, and nothing is logged. With Debug ticked, the log shows both directives waiting for the `late` store.",
			"Before the store exists, `Ping` does nothing and logs nothing.",
			"`Add the store` logs the store's creation, and the outside line switches to its message.",
			"`Ping` then increments the late store's pings.",
			"`Remove the store` logs its destruction. The outside line keeps the last message it showed, and `Ping` does nothing again.",
			"Adding it again creates a new store, the outside line binds to it, and its pings start from 0.",
		]}
	>
		<div class="space-y-3">
			<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm">
				<span class="text-muted" data-dom--text="late:$message">Waiting for the late store…</span>
				<button class="btn btn-sm ml-auto" data-events--click="late:@ping">Ping</button>
			</div>
			<div data-scopes-late-slot class="min-h-10"></div>
			<div class="flex gap-2">
				<button class="btn" data-scopes-add-late>Add the store</button>
				<button class="btn btn-ghost" data-scopes-remove-late>Remove the store</button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Scenario>

	<script>
		import "../../scripts/catalyst/scopes";
	</script>
</Playground>
